// review — dispatch a GitHub PR Item to a code review (items-spec I5,
// review-pipeline-spec RV3).
//
// The daemon dispatches this via POST /items/run: it resolves the PR
// Item to vars (repo, pr_number, url, title). The review is DIFF-BASED:
// `review_loop` runs the shared multi-lens review-core sub-pipeline inline
// via stack.manager_loop, seeding each lens's diff_cmd with `gh pr diff`.
// That reads the PR straight from the GitHub API, so it needs no local
// checkout and works under ANY runner — including a VM whose /work jj
// workspace has no `.git` (an earlier `gh pr checkout` node failed there,
// and even on the host it ran outside a git worktree: "not a git repository").
//
// `review_loop` seeds review-core's one input, diff_cmd, with the PR's
// diff command; the override's $context.pr_number/$context.repo are
// expanded against this run's context when the child is seeded. review-core
// fans out to five adversarial lenses and a `synth` verdict, whose outcome
// becomes the loop's outcome (a FAIL verdict fails the run).
//
//   attractor run review -var repo=owner/name -var pr_number=42 \
//     -var url=… -var title=…
digraph review {
    goal = "Review PR #$context.pr_number ($context.title) in $context.repo"
    vars = "repo,pr_number,url,title"
    max_node_visits = 2

    start [shape=Mdiamond]

    review_loop [type="stack.manager_loop",
                 stack.child_dotfile="../review-core/pipeline.dot",
                 stack.child.var.diff_cmd="gh pr diff $context.pr_number --repo $context.repo"]

    done [shape=Msquare]

    start -> review_loop
    review_loop -> done
}
